  "notes": "R24 targets rent activation rule. Primary evidence E1 and E2 from TOOLCHAIN-CONF-RENT-01 documents (v1.2 and base) consistently specify three core activation behaviors: (1) automatic status update to Active when rental start date is reached (2.4.1), (2) manual activation capability for authorized users (2.4.2), and (3) prevention of activation for non-Approved rents (2.4.3). E4 provides implementation context confirming the same specification. E6 and E7 provide availability management context showing how Active rents affect item availability. E10 and E11 show related rent creation flow implementation. No conflicts detected between versions. Authorization restriction on manual activation is a clear exception. Gaps exist around the interaction between automatic and manual activation paths, and behavior when preconditions are not met.",
